areas=[
('columbia','Columbia','City energy. A place of your own.','Downtown connections · Established neighborhoods','Columbia brings the state capital, the University of South Carolina, and distinct neighborhood settings into one home search. Start with the places you visit every day, then compare the streets and homes that connect them.','Compare downtown condominiums with detached homes in established neighborhoods. Consider parking, outdoor space, building maintenance, and how you actually travel to work.','For a condominium, request association documents, dues, parking assignments, and any rental restrictions. For an older house, prioritize the roof, foundation, wiring, and recent improvements.','Main Street, the Vista, and the university area offer different settings. Visit at different times of day to understand traffic, activity, and your preferred pace.','https://www.experiencecolumbiasc.com/'),
('lexington','Lexington','Room for your next chapter.','Town-center life · Lake Murray connections','Lexington is a useful starting point for buyers comparing town-center convenience with neighborhoods toward Lake Murray and the wider Lexington County area. The right location depends on your daily routes as much as your floor plan.','Compare established subdivisions, newer construction, and homes outside a subdivision. Separate the town limits from a Lexington mailing address when checking services.','Review HOA documents, construction warranties where applicable, and ongoing maintenance. Compare the total monthly cost, including association dues and insurance.','Drive your route along US 1, US 378, or SC 6 during the times you expect to travel. Explore the town center and local parks before deciding how close you want to be.','https://www.lexsc.gov/'),
('irmo','Irmo','Connected to the city. Close to the lake.','Northwest Midlands · Everyday convenience','Irmo offers a northwest Midlands starting point for exploring homes around the Columbia–Lake Murray corridor. Compare the exact address and daily drive rather than relying on a broad area label.','Look at established neighborhoods, yard size, renovation quality, and access to your regular shopping and recreation. A mailing address alone does not establish town boundaries.','Verify county, municipal services, association obligations, and assigned schools for each property. Compare road noise and driveway access in person.','Consider how your route connects to I-26 and the Harbison area. If lake recreation matters, compare actual access points rather than straight-line distance to the water.','https://www.townofirmosc.com/'),
('chapin','Chapin','A little more lake in your life.','Small-town setting · Lake-area living','Chapin is a starting point for buyers exploring the north side of Lake Murray. Compare homes close to town with properties farther along the lake roads: the setting and daily drive can feel very different.','Distinguish waterfront, water-view, community-access, and off-water homes. Each offers a different relationship to the lake and a different ownership checklist.','Confirm public water or well, sewer or septic, road access, and any association rules. If a property advertises a dock or lake access, verify the supporting documents.','Tour the route from the property to town and I-26. A home near the lake on a map may be a longer drive from the places you visit each day.','https://www.chapinsc.com/'),
('lake-murray','Lake Murray','Find your place by the water.','Waterfront · Water views · Lake access','Lake Murray is a regional search, not a single town. Compare shoreline locations around Lexington, Irmo, and Chapin while separating the view you love from the access and ownership details you need.','Decide whether you want private waterfront, a shared launch, a marina nearby, or simply a lake-area setting. Those choices can change your search considerably.','Ask about dock permits, shoreline restrictions, water depth, maintenance, and flood-zone information. Verify advertised access and permit status with the appropriate authority before relying on them.','Visit the property from both a daily-life and recreation perspective. Think through storage, boat access, exposure to sun, and the drive to work and services.','https://www.lakemurraycountry.com/'),
('west-columbia-cayce','West Columbia & Cayce','Across the river. Full of possibility.','River connections · Close-in neighborhoods','West Columbia and Cayce are distinct cities across the river from central Columbia. Explore them separately while comparing access to downtown, river recreation, and the roads you use most.','Compare established houses, renovated properties, and newer options by condition and location. Similar-looking homes can have very different maintenance histories.','Check municipal boundaries and services, drainage, and flood-zone information for the specific parcel. Proximity to the river is not a substitute for an address-level review.','Try your bridge crossing at commute time and explore the surrounding blocks on foot where practical. Consider how the home connects to the riverfront and your daily destinations.','https://www.experiencecolumbiasc.com/neighborhoods/')]
faqs=[('Who is James Nowlin?','James Nowlin is a real estate agent with Realty ONE Group Reside serving the Columbia metro area. His professional background includes mortgage finance. His published South Carolina license number is 129577.'),('How do I contact James?','Call or text (803) 949-0229, or email office@jamesnowlinrealtor.com. His brokerage office is listed at 5300-B Sunset Boulevard, Lexington, SC 29072.'),('Where should I start my Columbia-area home search?','Start with your budget, daily destinations, and the kind of home you want. Compare Columbia, Lexington, Irmo, Chapin, Lake Murray, and West Columbia or Cayce using the area guides, then ask James to help narrow the search.'),('Can I see current homes for sale?','Yes. The Search Homes links open James’s brokerage property search, where you can check available listings and current details. Property availability and prices can change; confirm them with James before planning a showing.'),('How can I find out what my home is worth?','Ask James for a property-specific market conversation. Recent comparable sales, condition, location, and competing inventory help inform a pricing strategy. An automated estimate is only a starting point.'),('What is different about buying near Lake Murray?','Waterfront, water-view, and lake-access properties are different categories. Review access rights, dock and shoreline requirements, water depth, and maintenance for the specific property before deciding.'),('Can James help me buy and sell at the same time?','Contact James to discuss your timing, current home, and next purchase. A coordinated plan should account for preparation, financing, contract deadlines, and possible gaps between closings.'),('How do I check school assignments?','Verify the exact property address directly with the relevant school district. Mailing addresses and real estate area names do not guarantee a particular school assignment.')]
def btn(text,url,cls=''):return f'<a class="button {cls}" href="{html.escape(url,quote=True)}">{text}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>'
def faqblock(items):return '<div class="faqs">'+''.join(f'<details><summary>{q}<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><p>{a}</p></details>' for q,a in items)+'</div>'
def area_cards():return '<div class="area-grid">'+''.join(f'<a class="area-card a{i}" href="/areas/{s}/"><span class="eyebrow">0{i+1} / THE MIDLANDS</span><h3>{n}</h3><p>{tag}</p><span class="circle" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>' for i,(s,n,h,tag,*_) in enumerate(areas))+'</div>'
