home='''<section class="hero"><img class="heroimg" src="/assets/hero.jpg" alt="Welcoming home illuminated at dusk" fetchpriority="high" width="1600" height="800"><div class="hero-content wrap"><p class="eyebrow">COLUMBIA, SOUTH CAROLINA & THE MIDLANDS</p><h1>Your Columbia &amp;<br>Lexington<br><em>Home Expert.</em></h1><p>Serving all of the Midlands, South Carolina.<br>Local guidance. Personal attention. A place to call home.</p><div class="actions">'''+btn('Find your home','/homes/','gold')+btn('Thinking of selling?','/sell/','outline')+'''</div></div><div class="hero-bottom wrap"><span>LOCAL CONNECTIONS. PERSONAL SERVICE.</span><a href="#explore">Explore what’s next ↓</a></div></section><div class="ribbon"><span>COLUMBIA</span><span>LEXINGTON</span><span>IRMO</span><span>CHAPIN</span><span>LAKE MURRAY</span><span>WEST COLUMBIA & CAYCE</span></div><section id="explore" class="wrap section"><div class="sectionhead"><div><p class="eyebrow">SIX STARTING POINTS. ENDLESS POSSIBILITIES.</p><h2>Where do you<br><em>feel at home?</em></h2></div><p>City streets or lake-area living. A familiar neighborhood or a fresh perspective. Get to know the places that make the Midlands home.</p></div>'''+area_cards()+'''</section><section class="aboutband"><div class="wrap split"><div class="portraitframe"><img src="/assets/portrait.png" alt="James Nowlin, real estate agent with Realty ONE Group Reside" width="319" height="319" loading="lazy"><span>YOUR AGENT. YOUR ADVOCATE.</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">MEET JAMES NOWLIN</p><h2>Good real estate<br>starts with <em>listening.</em></h2><p>Every move has a story. James brings a personal approach to helping buyers and sellers navigate the Columbia metro area—starting with what matters to you.</p><p>His background in mortgage finance brings attention to the details behind a move, alongside clear communication and a commitment to his clients’ goals.</p>'''+btn('Get to know James','/about/')+'''</div></div></section><section class="wrap section"><div class="sectionhead"><div><p class="eyebrow">A CLEAR PATH FORWARD</p><h2>Your move.<br><em>Your way.</em></h2></div><p>You don’t need every answer to take the first step. Start with the path that fits you.</p></div><div class="servicegrid"><a href="/buy/"><span class="eyebrow">01 / BUY WITH JAMES</span><h3>Find the right fit.</h3><p>Turn a wish list into a focused search, with a clear plan from first conversation to closing.</p><span class="textlink">Explore buying →</span></a><a href="/sell/"><span class="eyebrow">02 / SELL WITH JAMES</span><h3>Make your next move.</h3><p>Start with your home, your timing, and a thoughtful conversation about preparation and pricing.</p><span class="textlink">Explore selling →</span></a></div></section><section class="history"><div class="wrap section"><div class="sectionhead"><div><p class="eyebrow">A LOOK BACK</p><h2>Homes with<br><em>a next chapter.</em></h2></div><p>A selection of properties publicly attributed to James’s listing history. These are historical examples, not current offers for sale.</p></div><div class="propertyrows">'''+''.join(f'<a href="https://www.realty.com/real-estate-agents/2640598/james_nowlin"><span class="eyebrow">PAST LISTING</span><h3>{a}</h3><p>{c}</p><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>' for a,c in [('231 Chestnut Oak Lane','West Columbia, SC'),('324 Timbermill Drive','Lexington, SC'),('6627 Christie Road','Columbia, SC')])+'''</div><p class="fine">Source: Realty.com agent listing history, reviewed October 14, 2026. No sale price or transaction-side representation is implied.</p>'''+btn('Explore current homes','/homes/')+'''</div></section><section class="resource-home wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">SETTLE IN WITH CONFIDENCE</p><h2>Your Midlands<br><em>resource guide.</em></h2><p>Property records. Utilities. School districts. Lake permits.<br>Official local links and a practical moving checklist, all in one place.</p></div><a class="button" href="/resources/">Explore local resources <span>↗</span></a></section><section class="wrap section split faqsection"><div><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE CLARITY GOES A LONG WAY</p><h2>Good questions.<br><em>Straight answers.</em></h2><a class="textlink" href="/faq/">All frequently asked questions →</a></div>'''+faqblock(faqs[2:6])+'''</section>'''
